# Glific backend endpoints for the web-channel app.
#
# In most deployments you do NOT need to set these. One build serves every organisation, so the
# backend origin is derived at runtime from the hostname: the leading `web` label is swapped for
# `api`.
#
#   web.staging.glific.com  ->  api.staging.glific.com
#   web.tap.glific.com      ->  api.tap.glific.com
#
# Set them only when that derivation cannot work:
#
# VERCEL PREVIEW DEPLOYMENTS — required. A hostname like
# glific-web-channel-git-main-glific.vercel.app carries no organisation information, so there is
# nothing to derive from and the preview would fall back to same-origin paths that hit Vercel
# rather than Glific. Set both on the Preview environment:
#   VITE_GLIFIC_API_URL=https://api.staging.glific.com/api
#   VITE_WEB_SOCKET=wss://api.staging.glific.com/web_socket
#
# LOCAL DEV — leave unset. The app falls back to same-origin relative paths (/api, /web_socket)
# which the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts) forwards to the Glific backend. Change the proxy
# target there if your backend runs elsewhere.
#
# ANY OTHER HOST that is not `web.<something>.<tld>` — set them explicitly, for the same reason
# as the preview case.
#
# Note that VITE_GLIFIC_API_URL includes the /api suffix and VITE_WEB_SOCKET is a full ws(s) URL;
# they are used verbatim, not combined with anything.

# VITE_GLIFIC_API_URL=
# VITE_WEB_SOCKET=
